 3. 🔌 Why the internet suddenly broke 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Allie Carl/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Experts tell us this week's online outages were likely triggered by widespread efforts to fix outdated code, as institutions try to safeguard their systems from a potential hacking onslaught. 

 The administration  says the incidents don't appear linked to hacking or probing. Secretary of State Marco Rubio said in Manila: "We have zero evidence or any reason to believe that any of these isolated or individual instances have anything to do with nefarious actors, with cyber hackers, with criminals, with another nation-state, with a malign actor of any kind." The internet pointed fingers toward an AI agent doomsday, sending people into a frenzy that the Big One™ is coming, Axios' Josephine Walker writes. 

 👉 Downdetector data show that while the seven days through Monday represent the highest number of weekly outages in the past 12 months, the pattern over longer periods such as 30 days is far from unprecedented. Keep reading . 

 
 
