 4. 💰 Axios BFD: Don Jr.&#x27;s AI warning 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Axios' Dan Primack interviews Donald Trump Jr. (center) and 1789 Capital president Omeed Malik at our BFD summit in Manhattan yesterday. Photo: Sam Popp for Axios NEW YORK — Donald Trump Jr. told Axios' Dan Primack at our BFD summit in Manhattan yesterday that investors underestimated the political pushback to the AI ecosystem.

 Trump Jr. — appearing alongside 1789 Capital co-founder and president Omeed Malik, whose venture Trump Jr. joined in 2024 — said that "a lot of" the pushback "is manufactured." But "that doesn't mean it's not real." "I think some of the big founders of the biggest [AI] companies out there probably have not done themselves the best service as [a] marketing department," Don Jr. said, adding that they're "probably not the best messengers when they basically say, 'AI is gonna rule the world, and you should be thrilled about it.'" Primack pressed Don Jr. on accusations of self-dealing by the president's family and allies. "The notion that I should somehow sit in a corner, suck my thumb, and wait, you know, 8 years, in this case, 12 years, 'til we're out of the political game, it's not real," Trump Jr. said.

 Asked if he understands why people question 1789 Capital investing in companies that receive government contracts, Trump Jr., a senior partner at the Florida-based firm, replied: "I can see what they're saying. It doesn't make it so." ⚡ More top moments from BFD: Goldman sees "mini-bubbles" ... A-Rod on WNBA "hypergrowth" ... Luxury's next era ... AI and rate hikes . 

 
 
