 7. 🚀 Toyota&#x27;s final frontier 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Joann Muller and Thomas Novelly — authors of our Future of Mobility and Future of Defense newsletters — write: 

 Toyota — the Japanese industrial giant that evolved from making textile looms to building cars — is exploring another potentially transformative business opportunity: space.

 Why it matters: The booming space industry has a manufacturing problem — and Toyota thinks it can help solve it. As demand for satellites soars, Toyota sees an opportunity to apply its expertise in efficient, high-volume manufacturing to an industry that has traditionally relied on expensive, custom-built spacecraft.

 In an exclusive interview with Axios, Toyota revealed that it has invested more than $240 million in 11 space-related startups. Keep reading . 

 
 
