 8. 🎮 1 fun thing: Getting &quot;GTA Flu&quot; 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Promotional branding for "Grand Theft Auto VI" on the Kaseya Center in Miami, the inspiration for the game's fictional Vice City. Photo: Alfonso Duran/Bloomberg via Getty Images "Grand Theft Auto VI," perhaps the year's biggest cultural phenomenon, goes live at midnight tonight, Axios' Herb Scribner writes. 

 30% of U.S. employees are considering taking time off to play, according to GameSquare research shared with Axios. Of those workers, 36% say they might call out sick — a trend becoming known as the "GTA Flu." Zoom in: The U.S. Army is offering eligible soldiers four days off to play as a reenlistment incentive. Logitech is giving its 7,000 employees a paid day off. A college professor canceled homework.

 Even birdwatchers, apparently, are buying the game just to look at its virtual birds. Go deeper : What to know about the game. 

 
 
